  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nEnsembles are in good agreement the Pacific low will slowly drift\neast northeastward across far northern Arizona and southern Utah \non Tuesday before most of the energy exits to the northeast on \nWednesday. Additional dry air will spread across the region from \nthe northwest during this time with PWATs dropping to 75% of \nnormal and skies clearing out later on Tuesday. Behind the cold \nfront on Tuesday, temperatures will dip further with NBM forecast \nhighs only in the mid 70s Tuesday, or 10-15 degrees below normal. \nOvernight lows Tuesday night/Wednesday morning are also expected \nto fall well into the 50s for the bulk of the area to as cool as \nthe mid to upper 40s for rural lower desert and higher terrain \nlocations. \n\nModel guidance is still somewhat uncertain with the eventual \nplacement of the incoming upper level ridge and a likely lingering\ntrough axis and/or cut-off low that should form late week. No \nmatter the eventual evolution, our weather will basically stay the\nsame with dry conditions prevailing late week into next weekend. \nTemperatures will moderate some late week with highs returning \ninto the 80s, but likely staying below normal. We may end up \nhaving another back-door cool front moving into the area from the \neast by Friday or Saturday and this should either maintain or cool\noff temperatures going into next weekend. As with any backdoor \nfront, gusty easterly winds are likely to follow as well and with \nthe potential cutoff low in the area, easterly winds in this case\nmay become quite strong. Global models are already showing \npotential for some very strong, advisory level or higher, winds \nacross southeast AZ.",
